BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art of the "REandMIX"
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261128T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261128T220000
UID:008e744b43f8fbbdf23a41571d4b9db3@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:Death of Caesar Fine Arts Gallery hosts J Read's "Art of the R
 EadMIX" production. This show features some of the most prominent\, season
 ed\, and talented artists that have been making waves in the tristate area
  for at least the past 10 years! J Read is an eclectic artist\, author\, a
 nd musician who plays the violin\, sings\, and raps. Mikumari is a renown 
 poet and emcee originally from D.C. who has been pioneering unique pieces 
 and performance styles in and around NY/NJ since the early 2000's. Lyle Om
 olayo is an emcee\, visual artist\, and animator from Plainfield\, NJ who 
 is one half of the world traveled rap duo "Negros Americanos". Last and ce
 rtainly not least\, Maurice Chestnut is an elite poet and tap dancer who h
 as shared stages with some of the greatest dancers and artists of our gene
 ration This event will also feature visual art from Montclair's own\, Brez
 aja Monét\, who is a well studied\, artist\, photographer and videographe
 r who graduated VCU\, and went on to work with New Balance\, making major 
 contributions in their design department. She is now an independent artist
  who is expanding her visual art to include ceramics\, which can be seen f
 eatured at Montclair Mud Clay Studio. THEME: SHOWCASE HOST: J Read FEATURE
 S: Mikumari / Lyle Omolayo / Maurice Chestnut / Brezaja Monét PRICE: TICK
 ETS $20 - https://www.eventbrite.com/e/art-of-the-readmix-tickets-20039723
 11128 CONTACT: FB - Jared J Read Fontaine
LOCATION:Fine Arts Studio\, 101 Glenridge Avenue\, Montclair\, NJ\, 07042
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/art-of-the-reandmix
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
